---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import SiteLink from '../components/SiteLink.astro';
import { APP_NAME, BUSINESS_NAME, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../utils/env';

const effectiveDateISO = '2026-08-29';
const effectiveDateLabel = 'August 29, 2026';
---

<Doc
  title="Privacy"
  description={`How ${APP_NAME} handles data.`}
>
  <header class="doc__header">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
  </header>

  <p>{APP_NAME} is published by {BUSINESS_NAME}.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      {APP_NAME} sends usage information to <SiteLink href="https://telemetrydeck.com/privacy/" target="_blank" aria-label="TelemetryDeck privacy policy, opens in new tab">TelemetryDeck</SiteLink>. That covers how you
      use the app, what you buy, crashes, how well the app runs, and details
      about your app, device, and settings. Those details include your
      accessibility settings, color scheme, language, layout direction, and
      region. We use all of it to see how people play and to make the app
      better.
    </p>
    <p>
      The app also makes a random ID for your copy of {APP_NAME} and sends a
      scrambled version of it. That ID stays the same until you reset the app's
      data or delete the app.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can turn analytics off in the app's settings. That stops new
      information from being sent. It does not delete what was already sent. We
      do not set a date for deleting old records, and those records have no name
      or email in them, so we cannot find one person's records to delete.
    </p>
    <p>
      TelemetryDeck has to protect this data at least as well as this policy and
      Apple's rules require.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Content reports</h2>
    <p>
      If you send us a content report, the email includes your reason, the round
      ID, the app version, and the build number. It comes from your own email
      account, so we get that email address too. Your drawing is included only
      if you choose to attach it. We use all of this to look into what you
      reported.
    </p>
    <p>
      We keep report emails in our support inbox. You can ask us to delete yours
      by emailing <SiteLink href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</SiteLink> from the address you sent it from.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Tracking</h2>
    <p>
      No one uses {APP_NAME} to track what you do on other websites or in other
      companies' apps.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If we make important changes to this policy, we will post them on this
      page.
    </p>
  </section>

  <footer class="doc__meta">Effective <time datetime={effectiveDateISO}>{effectiveDateLabel}</time>.</footer>
</Doc>
